          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %strong> Double gluing
            , coupled with orthogonality, is a method for creating new models of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+logic"} linear logic
            such as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star-polycategories"} star-polycategories
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star-autonomous+categories"} star-autonomous categories
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Artin+gluing"} Artin gluing
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+spaces"} phase spaces
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherence+spaces"} coherence spaces
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finiteness+spaces"} finiteness spaces
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/totality+spaces"} totality spaces
            = succeed "." do
              %span.newWikiWord
                probabilistic coherence spaces
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/probabilistic+coherence+spaces"} ?
          %p
            Although the name presumably refers to gluing along “two functors at once”, it turns out to also be closely connected to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+categories"} double categories
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+double+categories"} comma double categories
          %h2#double_gluing_along_homsets_with_orthogonality Double gluing along hom-sets with orthogonality
          %h3#coherence_spaces_via_double_gluing Coherence spaces via double gluing
          %p
            We begin with the definition of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherence+spaces"} coherence spaces
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u\subset X
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v\subseteq X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                  %mo ⊥
                  %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u\perp v
            if
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi u
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ≤
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |u\cap v|\leq 1
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\subseteq P(X)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi U
                      %mo ⊥
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi v
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                    %mo ∀
                    %mi u
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi U
                    %mo .
                    %mi u
                    %mo ⊥
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {U}^\perp=\{v \subseteq X \mid \forall u \in U. u \perp v\}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherence+space"} coherence space
            can be given by a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            together with a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\subseteq P(X)
            of cliques and a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V\subseteq P(X)
            of co-cliques that are orthogonal in the sense that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mo ⊥
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U=V^\perp
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi U
                      %mo ⊥
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V=U^\perp
          %p
            In this presentation of coherence spaces, we can regard
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
            as a relation
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\to X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
            as a relation
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mo ⊥
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to \bot
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊥
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \perp
            is then a family of subsets
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊥
                      %mi X
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mo ⊥
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \perp_X\subseteq [1\to X]\times [X\to \bot]
          %h3#general_definition_of_double_gluing_along_homsets_with_tight_orthogonality General definition of double gluing along hom-sets with tight orthogonality
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
            with an object
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi I
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I^*
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊥
                    %mi X
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi I
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi I
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \perp_X\subseteq C(I,X)\times C(X,I^*)
